3	// Listens to OrcaSlicer's own dialogs. Every Orca dialog opens through
4	// DPIAware::ShowModal, which first asks answer_modal (GUI_Utils.hpp); that
5	// hands the dialog to the listeners registered here, innermost first. A
6	// listener answers the dialog, and it is never shown, or passes it on; when
7	// every listener has passed, Orca shows it as usual.
8	//
9	// A listener learns what the window itself shows: its title, its message and
10	// which of the standard buttons it offers. Nothing is matched against the
11	// words, which are Orca's and in the interface language.
12	//
13	// GUI thread only.
